          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you, my father and king, as my filial bond requires—no more and no less.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Cordelia directly avows a loving emotional state toward Lear. The qualification defines its proper measure rather than removing its truth-conditional force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The avowal explicitly invokes Cordelia's existing filial bond and thereby affirms the duties of love, obedience, and honour that she owes Lear. This is an enactment or renewal of a daughter’s relational obligation, not a new promise of unlimited devotion. Lear does not accept this formulation as sufficient and urges her to revise it.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I\\nReturn those duties back as are right fit,\\nObey you, love you, and most honour you.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Mend your speech a little,\\nLest you may mar your fortunes.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The focal expression is a controlled, carefully delimited answer to Lear’s demand, not a reflex-like affective discharge. Cordelia expressly frames her response in measured terms.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"According to my bond; no more nor less.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"reason\":\"No substantial residual core force is needed: the expression’s avowal is covered by T, while its invocation of filial duty is covered by P. Its contrastive refusal to exaggerate shapes those modes rather than constituting a separate one.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"}]} },\"original_speech_situation\":\"Lear publicly asks his daughters to say which loves him most while allocating portions of his kingdom. After refusing inflated rhetoric, Cordelia answers that she loves him according to her filial bond, neither more nor less. She distinguishes this filial love and duty from the love she may owe a future husband. Lear treats her answer as inadequate and warns that it will damage her fortunes.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"Cordelia invokes and affirms her existing obligations as Lear’s daughter: to love, obey, honour, and return fitting duties to him. She does not promise exclusive or unlimited love and explicitly reserves part of her future love, care, and duty for a husband. Lear rejects her formulation as insufficient rather than accepting it as the declaration he demanded.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passages are recognisable as Shakespeare’s King Lear, especially the opening love test and Cordelia’s reunion with Lear. The classification relies only on the supplied blocks.\",\"limitations\":\"The target modernises and shortens Cordelia’s actual wording, omitting the crucial qualification “According to my bond; no more nor less.” The supplied later passages strongly support genuine affection through her concern, care, forgiveness, and grief, but they do not make the focal utterance a promise or an expressive outburst.\"}"
        }
      ],
